{"kind":"request","text":"Gate warning for implementation notes and evidence paths (PD-2 item 8 of ruling fcab078d; tech-debt review 72a6df7d)\n\nSource: docs/testing.md on Main 2aaba5e4, subsection \"The implementation note and its evidence\". The rule says a gate step warns, and does not fail, on a note over 40 KB or on a new path under notes/implementation/evidence/ that is not a manifest. Until it exists the checker applies the rule by hand.\n\nWork: one builder head. A script (for example scripts/check-notes.mjs) reads the commits in base..HEAD with the same base the commit-message check uses, and prints one warning line for each added or changed file under notes/implementation/ over 40,960 bytes, and for each added path under notes/implementation/evidence/ whose name does not end in .manifest.json. It exits 0 in both cases; the gate prints its lines in the step summary. A Node test covers the three cases (large note, non-manifest evidence path, clean head) with fixture commits. scripts/gate.sh gains the step after doc-links. docs/testing.md names the step in its gate paragraph and in the subsection above.\n\nAcceptance: the script warns on each case and never fails the gate; the Node test passes; the gate passes at the reviewed head; the head carries its implementation note and manifest under the rule; one checker review at the exact head before landing. Place: after 3e01b385 lands; before BR-3. Size: small.","body":{"conditions":"Warning only, never a gate failure; Node test for the three cases; gate passes; the head carries its note and manifest; one checker review at the exact head before landing.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}